    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's a \"natural response\" but that doesnt make it any less exhausting. it just feels like i've been playing a game where all the rules were fake. everything i thought gave me purpose was just an illusion. honestly, it makes me wonder if there's even a point to trying to fix it or find new \"rules.\" if the foundation is gone, why bother building anything else?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's exhausting because you're trying to process a complete re-evaluation of your reality, and that takes immense energy. The question of whether to rebuild when the foundation is gone is a very big one, but perhaps the answer isn't about building something new right away. Sometimes, the most necessary step is simply acknowledging the void, allowing yourself to exist in the uncertainty without the pressure to find a grand purpose immediately.",
      "source": "target",
